:"MSST","oppName":"Mississippi State Bulldogs","result":"W","score":"31-3","values":[8,4,4,3,2,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,0]},{"id":"401856743","date":"2026-11-07","week":10,"type":"reg","home":false,"opp":"MIZ","oppName":"Missouri Tigers","result":"W","score":"34-20","values":[6,3,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2]}]}},"summaryLabel":"2026 season stats","news":[{"headline":"Wake Forest's post-blowout jab at SMU tops college football Week 11 trolls","description":"Wake Forest dominated SMU on the gridiron Saturday -- and added insult to injury after the game.","published":"2026-11-14T23:36:57.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481104/college-football-trolls-week-11","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Watch best moments and top plays live from Week 11","published":"2026-11-14T23:16:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50474063/week-11-live-highlights","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Darian Mensah dices up ex-team Duke as Miami rebounds from first loss","description":"Miami quarterback Darian Mensah diced up his former team Saturday, finishing with 382 yards and a touchdown in the 36-25 victory over Duke.","published":"2026-11-14T23:57:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50484151/darian-mensah-dices-ex-team-duke-miami-rebounds-first-loss","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest strengthens CFP case with 'statement' win at SMU","description":"No. 13 Wake Forest made a statement to the College Football Playoff selection committee with a 49-7 blowout of SMU on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-15T00:41:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50483729/wake-forest-strengthens-cfp-case-statement-win-smu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Vols lose top receiver Matthews to knee injury vs. Texas A&M","description":"Tennessee leading receiver Mike Matthews suffered a right knee injury in the second quarter of Saturday's game at Texas A&M.","published":"2026-11-14T23:16:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50483677/vols-lose-top-receiver-matthews-knee-injury-vs-texas-am","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia commit, DL Marcellus Young Casario died after 'sudden medical emergency'","description":"Marcellus Young Casario, a Georgia football commit, died Friday after experiencing a \"sudden medical emergency,\" according to his high school.","published":"2026-11-14T20:36:58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482223/georgia-football-commit-marcellus-young-casario-dies-suddenly","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma AD rips Ole Miss, SEC; Rebels defend travel effort","description":"Oklahoma AD Roger Denny ripped the SEC and Ole Miss for the \"inexplicable\" decision to move its game to Sunday, while the Rebels defended their travel efforts.","published":"2026-11-14T23:54:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482206/oklahoma-ad-infuriated-sec-ole-miss-sunday-game","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Clemson QB Reynolds to have MRI on knee; backup Vizzina (ankle) also hurt","description":"Clemson quarterback Tait Reynolds is having an MRI on his injured knee, and backup Christopher Vizzina was sent to the hospital to evaluate his ankle.","published":"2026-11-14T23:52:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482105/clemson-qb-tait-reynolds-suffers-leg-injury-slide","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Central Oklahoma AD trolls Ole Miss amid FAA crisis-forced kickoff change","description":"The Division II school offered Ole Miss fans attending its Oklahoma matchup free admission due to the kickoff date change.","published":"2026-11-14T22:28:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481529/central-oklahoma-troll-ole-miss-faa-decsion","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State WR Smith sets Big Ten record, states Heisman case","description":"Ohio State wide receiver Jeremiah Smith broke yet another record, eclipsing the Big Ten mark for career receiving yards while also making his Heisman Trophy case in Saturday's win over Northwestern.","published":"2026-11-14T23:15:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481134/ohio-state-jeremiah-smith-sets-big-ten-receiving-record","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4922981/rasheem-biles","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rasheem_Biles"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Rasheem Biles","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rasheem_Biles","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:23Z","intro":"Rasheem Biles (born November 18, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the Texas Longhorns. He previously played for the Pittsburgh Panthers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Biles attended Pickerington High School Central in Pickerington, Ohio, where he played wide receiver, running back and defensive back. As a senior he played in five games due to injury and had over 400 all-purpose yards and five total touchdowns including two interceptions returned for touchdown. As a junior he had 74 tackles and three interceptions with two returned for a touchdown. Biles committed to the University of Pittsburgh to play college."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"PITTSBURGH\nAs a true freshman at Pittsburgh in 2023, Biles played in nine games and tied a school record with three blocked punts. He became a starter his sophomore year in 2024, starting nine of 12 games and recording 82 tackles, 5.5 sacks and an interception which he returned for a touchdown. He returned to Pittsburgh as a starter in 2025, playing in 10 games and recording 101 tackles, 4.5 sacks, two interceptions, both returned for touchdowns, two forced fumbles, and one fumble recovery, returned for a touchdown. At the end of the season, Biles entered the transfer portal.\n\nTEXAS\nOn January 10, 2026, Biles committed to Texas. In Week 9 against Mississippi State, Biles recorded eight tackles, including three sacks and four tackles for a loss, and two forced fumbles, earning SEC Co-Defensive Player of the Week for his performance."}]}}